

3. Shot Clock / Passive Play Indicator

Handball doesn’t have a strict shot clock, but referees signal passive play.

You can add:

    A “Passive Play” toggle

    A 6‑pass counter (referees count passes after passive warning)

    A visual indicator on the display

This is extremely useful for commentators and streams.
4. Player Numbers for Goals

Optional but very nice:

    When a goal is scored, allow entering the scorer’s number

    Store a match log

    Display “Goal #23” briefly on the scoreboard

    Export match stats later

5. Match Log / Event Timeline

Handball is event‑rich. A timeline could include:

    Goals

    Suspensions

    Timeouts

    Period changes

    Technical timeouts

    End of half

This can be a simple list in the control panel.
6. Technical Timeout Button

For injuries, floor cleaning, or referee decisions.

    Stops the clock

    Marks the event in the log

    Optional countdown (e.g., 1 minute)

7. Automatic Period Transition Logic

You already have basic period switching, but handball has:

    1st half (30 min)

    10‑minute break

    2nd half (30 min)

    5‑minute break

    Overtime 1 (5 min)

    1‑minute break

    Overtime 2 (5 min)

    7‑meter shootout

You can automate:

Auto‑start break timer Auto‑switch to next period Auto‑prepare shootout mode
8. 7‑Meter Shootout Mode

A dedicated mode for penalty shootouts:

    Track each team’s attempts

    Mark goals/misses

    Display shootout score separately

    Sudden‑death logic

This is a huge upgrade for tournament play.
9. Team Logos

You already added color pickers — logos are the next step.

